# Integrated Stateful Agents

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"},
  {:runic_ai, path: "~/wrk/runic_ai"}
])

Code.require_file("support/runic_ai_livebook.exs", __DIR__)
```

## Purpose

External-state recipes return `Agent.State` and ask the caller to pass it into
the next turn. Integrated recipes keep agent lanes inside workflow-owned
`RunicAI.Integrated.RuntimeState`.

Use integrated state when you need:

* long-lived addressable agent lanes
* queued signals
* multiple agents in one workflow
* waits and review resumes indexed by resume key
* runtime sessions that can be supervised and persisted

## Provider Setup

```elixir
setup = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.inputs()
```

```elixir
model = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.read_model!(setup)
llm_opts = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.llm_opts(model, max_output_tokens: RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.read_max_output_tokens(setup))
```

## Build Two Agent Lanes

```elixir
alias RunicAI.Recipes.IntegratedChatAgent

integrated_workflow =
  IntegratedChatAgent.new(
    model: model,
    llm_opts: llm_opts,
    agents: [
      [id: "alpha", system: "You are alpha. Be analytical."],
      [id: "beta", system: "You are beta. Be concise."]
    ]
  )

RunicAI.Livebook.WorkflowViz.tabs(integrated_workflow)
```

## Route Signals To Different Agents

```elixir
RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.require_openai_key!()

integrated_run =
  integrated_workflow
  |> Runic.Workflow.react_until_satisfied(%{agent_id: "alpha", user: "Remember that my API is rate limited."})
  |> Runic.Workflow.react_until_satisfied(%{agent_id: "beta", user: "Remember that my UI is mobile first."})
  |> Runic.Workflow.react_until_satisfied(%{agent_id: "alpha", user: "What constraint did I give you?"})
  |> Runic.Workflow.react_until_satisfied(%{agent_id: "beta", user: "What constraint did I give you?"})

Kino.DataTable.new(
  Enum.map(IntegratedChatAgent.emissions(integrated_run), fn emission ->
    %{
      agent_id: emission.agent_id,
      kind: emission.kind,
      value: inspect(emission.value, limit: 4)
    }
  end)
)
```

```elixir
Kino.Layout.tabs(
  Runtime: Kino.Tree.new(IntegratedChatAgent.runtime_state(integrated_run)),
  Alpha: Kino.Tree.new(IntegratedChatAgent.session(integrated_run, "alpha")),
  Beta: Kino.Tree.new(IntegratedChatAgent.session(integrated_run, "beta"))
)
```

## Interactive Multi-Lane Chat

Use `alpha` and `beta` in the Agent id field and notice that each lane keeps its
own conversation.

```elixir
RunicAI.Livebook.Chat.start_integrated(
  IntegratedChatAgent,
  [
    model: model,
    llm_opts: llm_opts,
    agents: [
      [id: "alpha", system: "You are alpha. Be analytical."],
      [id: "beta", system: "You are beta. Be concise."]
    ]
  ],
  agent_id: "alpha",
  initial_message: "Remember that my service is rate limited."
)
```
